ct it can have when the  community and the  and the alumni and the former players  all can kind of come together and be  a part of the program and and  and i know i just know the effect it can  have on the guys as well  and the players and the appreciation  because you know  if if we can get the guys to have former  players come and talk to them  and just share their stories and their  experiences  it doesn't do anything but strengthen  that love and that bond with unlv  because while you're doing it as a  player that you know time goes fast  and things are moving and always you  know you're kind of here to there and  and just kind of still trying to figure  out life and and figure things out  but when a former player can kind of  come and tell you you know hey in 15  years  you know the best nights i still have  are when we get back together  and we and we watch a rebel game or we  or we share stories or  you know those reunions and we you know  we talk about coming to practice and  supporting you guys or  we look forward to a game on a calendar  each year when we all get back together  and  and just kind of impress that upon the  team and the players and  and just let them know how important it  is not just for now and  and that continued gel of the team for  you know  current success but how it can go going  forward 15 20 years down the line in  their life  what kind of rebel basketball team do  you see yourself coaching what style  honestly like we've talked about i i  just think  i think we've just got to have a team  that when when our opponent leaves the  game  and their coaches are in the their  locker room they're saying man those  guys love to play  those guys love to compete they love to  play for each other  they play so hard you know you can tell  that they they hate to lose  and um you know i just vis i don't  envision necessarily you know a running  gun or a full court press per se  at this point in time but i do envision  just  just diving on the flo